
Practical 1: Data Privacy Audit of LinkedIn

Aim

To conduct a data privacy audit of LinkedIn and identify possible privacy risks in its data collection and protection practices.

 Platform Selected

Organization: LinkedIn
Website: LinkedIn
Privacy Policy: LinkedIn Privacy Policy

 Requirements

Internet connection
Web browser
LinkedIn account (optional)

 Procedure

• Visit the LinkedIn website.

• Open its Privacy Policy.

• Check the types of personal data collected.

• Examine the use of cookies and tracking technologies.

• Check data sharing with third parties.

• Examine available privacy and security controls.

• Identify possible privacy risks.

• Suggest measures to improve privacy.

Observations:-

• LinkedIn collects PII such as name, email, phone number, location and professional information.

• IP address, device information and usage data** may also be collected.

• User data is used for personalization, recommendations, analytics and service improvement.

• Cookies and tracking technologies are used for analytics, personalization and advertising.

• Some information may be processed by third-party service providers and data processors


• Public profile information such as education, skills and employment details may be visible to other users depending on privacy settings.

• LinkedIn provides authentication and security controls** to protect user accounts.

• Personal data may be retained for legal, operational and security purposes.

 Privacy Risks Identified

• Possible PII exposure in case of a security breach.

• Tracking of user activity through cookies and pixels.

• User profiling based on professional information and activity.

• Third-party processing of user information.

• Exposure of professional information through **public profiles**.

 Recommendations

• Avoid sharing unnecessary personal information.

• Review privacy and profile-visibility settings.

• Enable Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA)

• Review cookie and tracking preferences.

• Avoid connecting unknown third-party applications.

• Use a strong and unique password.

Result

The Data Privacy Audit of LinkedIn was successfully performed and major areas such as PII collection, tracking technologies, third-party processing, profile visibility and security controls were identified.

Conclusion

LinkedIn provides privacy and security controls, but users should be careful about PII, tracking, public profile information and third-party data processing.
